SUMMARY:The In Town Throwdown w/ Moon Hunter
DESCRIPTION:An Afternoon Grill Out w/Live Music from Moon HunterStaying in town for Memorial Day weekend? Come hang with us in the yard for a casual afternoon of live music\, free food\, and cheap brews.\nMoon Hunter is a genre-blending powerhouse born from the union of David & Stephanie Irvine and Howie Neal of Moonbeatz\, The Project & The Lads\, and Andy & Ruthie Hunter of Soul Blue\, and Andy and Ruthie Hunter Music. Together\, these five seasoned musicians bring decades of groove\, grit\, and heart to the stage. Their sound spans classic rock\, southern rock\, swampy blues\, soulful country\, rootsy Americana\, and the rich storytelling traditions of folk-rock and country-rock. Come ready to dance\, reminisce\, and feel every note.Free to attend.*Burgers & Dogs While Supplies Last\n  \n\n\n‘The Mule’ – Tasting Room \n\n\n\n\n\nSay hello to The Mule – a full-service bar/event space in the home of Devil’s Foot Beverage’s production facility. Draft soda\, beer\, & wine – as well as delicious cocktails & mocktails featuring Devil’s Foot craft sodas and the largest collection of NC-made spirits in Asheville – all at your fingertips just outside of Biltmore Village! Open now for all of your beverage & party needs! devilsfootbrew.com/the-mule
URL:https://livemusicasheville.com/calendar/the-in-town-throwdown-w-moon-hunter/
LOCATION:The Mule at Devils Foot Beverages\, 131 Sweeten Creek Road\, Asheville\, NC\, 28803\, United States
CATEGORIES:Asheville Area,Live Music
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://livemusicasheville.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Screenshot-2026-05-06-071940-e1778066426626.png
GEO:35.5588369;-82.5218977
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=The Mule at Devils Foot Beverages 131 Sweeten Creek Road Asheville NC 28803 United States;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=131 Sweeten Creek Road:geo:-82.5218977,35.5588369
END:VEVENT
